{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note_main",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": -180 },
      "style": { "width": 1420, "height": 165 },
      "width": 1420, "height": 165,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 2,
          "text": "**MC P(water) Sensitivity vs Spectral Water Indices**  ·  from `sensitivity_option_c.py`\n\nQuantile-binned mean ± P10–P90 of P(water) as a function of NDWI / MNDWI / AWEI / MBWI. Spearman r measures monotone correlation.\n\n**Setup (ACOLITE L2W individual-band TIFs)**\n1. `water_prob_mc.tif` → **MC Probability** reader.\n2. Six Rrs_*.tif files → individual band readers (Blue=492 nm, Green=559, Red=665, NIR=833, SWIR1=1610, SWIR2=2186).\n3. Five `geo_band_stack` nodes merge them into [B1=Blue, B2=Green, B3=Red, B4=NIR, B5=SWIR1, B6=SWIR2].\n4. Files are already Rrs (sr⁻¹) — **no DN normalization needed**. Negative values on dark water pixels are normal.\n5. The **Spectral Indices** node computes NDWI + MNDWI + AWEI + MBWI.  Run — the Python node renders the 4-panel sensitivity figure."
        }
      }
    },

    {
